.SH NAME
git-work-issue-archive - Archive an issue


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-work issue archive ID [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Archive an issue: set its archived field, which is one of the three fields
every issue has. This is the replicated removal, the one that reaches every
clone; rm only deletes the local ref.
ID is an id prefix or an alias.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print the operations that would be committed, and write nothing

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for archive


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-work-issue(1)\fP
